    "fact": "A handle is 1-15 of [A-Za-z0-9_], not digits only, with an optional leading @; home, i, messages, notifications, settings, search and explore are X's own paths, not handles. A numeric user id is refused with a fix to pass the handle. A profile URL may carry a tab path (/with_replies, /media, /highlights, /articles, /lists, /followers, /following, /verified_followers, /followers_you_follow); the target is still the handle (source P2 R8 for the tab paths).",
    "cases": [
      {"input": "@example_user", "expected": {"handle": "example_user"}},
      {"input": "example_user", "expected": {"handle": "example_user"}},
      {"input": "Example_User", "expected": {"handle": "Example_User"}},
      {"input": "a", "expected": {"handle": "a"}},
      {"input": "abcdefghijklmno", "expected": {"handle": "abcdefghijklmno"}},
      {"input": "abcdefghijklmnop", "refused": "invalid handle"},
      {"input": "bad-handle", "refused": "invalid handle"},
      {"input": "@", "refused": "invalid handle"},
      {"input": "1234567890", "refused": "numeric user id: pass the handle"},
